Specification Common Mark

Attributes MarkdownRendering
| Name     | DataType |
| Markdown | String   |
| Html     | String   |
| Notes    | String   |

ScenarioGroup Paragraphs

Calculation  Render Plain Paragraph
Description Plain text is rendered as a paragraph.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown    | Html               | Notes                  |
| Hello world | <p>Hello world</p> | Single-line paragraph. |
| CommonMark  | <p>CommonMark</p>  | Simple text.           |

ScenarioGroup Headings

Calculation Render ATX Headings
Description Hash characters create headings.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown    | Html             | Notes            |
| # Heading   | <h1>Heading</h1> | Level 1 heading. |
| ## Heading  | <h2>Heading</h2> | Level 2 heading. |
| ### Heading | <h3>Heading</h3> | Level 3 heading. |

ScenarioGroup Emphasis

Calculation Render Emphasis
Description Asterisks create emphasis and strong emphasis.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown   | Html                                  | Notes            |
| *text*     | <p><em>text</em></p>                  | Emphasis.        |
| **text**   | <p><strong>text</strong></p>          | Strong emphasis. |
| ***text*** | <p><em><strong>text</strong></em></p> | Nested emphasis. |

ScenarioGroup Links

Calculation Render Links
Description Markdown links are rendered as anchor elements.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown                     | Html                                           | Notes         |
| [Home](/)                    | <p><a href="/">Home</a></p>                    | Relative URL. |
| [Google](https://google.com) | <p><a href="https://google.com">Google</a></p> | Absolute URL. |

ScenarioGroup Lists

Calculation Render Unordered Lists
Description Dash-prefixed items become unordered lists.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html                          | Notes        |
| - A      | <ul><li>A</li></ul>           | Single item. |
| - A\n- B | <ul><li>A</li><li>B</li></ul> | Two items.   |

Calculation Render Ordered Lists
Description Number-prefixed items become ordered lists.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown   | Html                          | Notes        |
| 1. A       | <ol><li>A</li></ol>           | Single item. |
| 1. A\n2. B | <ol><li>A</li><li>B</li></ol> | Two items.   |

ScenarioGroup Code

Calculation  Render Inline Code
Description Backticks create inline code.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html                     | Notes        |
| `code`   | <p><code>code</code></p> | Inline code. |

ScenarioGroup Block Quotes

Calculation  Render Block Quote
Description Greater-than signs create block quotes.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html                                   | Notes               |
| > quoted | <blockquote><p>quoted</p></blockquote> | Simple block quote. |

ScenarioGroup Escaping

Calculation Render Escaped Characters
Description Escaped formatting characters are rendered literally.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html          | Notes                  |
| \*text\* | <p>*text*</p> | Asterisks are literal. |

ScenarioGroup Horizontal Rules

Calculation Render Horizontal Rule
Description Three dashes create a thematic break.
Examples: MarkdownRendering
| Markdown | Html   | Notes            |
| ---      | <hr /> | Horizontal rule. |

ScenarioGroup Complex Documents

Scenario Render Shopping List Document
Description A document containing a heading and list.

Given Markdown
"""
# Shopping List

- Milk
- Bread
"""
When Markdown Is Rendered
Then Html Is
"""
<h1>Shopping List</h1>
<ul>
<li>Milk</li>
<li>Bread</li>
</ul>
"""

Scenario Render Complex Document
Description Multiple Markdown constructs are rendered in a single document.

Given Markdown
"""
# CommonMark

Welcome to **CommonMark**.

> Important note

- Item 1
- *Item 2*

Use `code`.
"""
When Markdown Is Rendered
Then Html Is
"""
<h1>CommonMark</h1>
<p>Welcome to <strong>CommonMark</strong>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Important note</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>Item 1</li>
<li><em>Item 2</em></li>
</ul>
<p>Use <code>code</code>.</p>
"""
